#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
rate_card.py — IDEAS Company Master Rate Card & Salary Master

Version: 6.0

This script contains the master RATE_CARD, TYPICAL_TEAMS, and SALARY_MASTER
dictionaries for the IDEAS pricing engine. It is separated for maintainability
and to provide a single source of truth for all role-based pricing information.

This module defines:
- RATE_CARD: A dictionary mapping all company roles to their respective allowances,
  including positional, skill, and daily.
- TYPICAL_TEAMS: A dictionary defining standard team compositions for various
  project types, used for automated cost estimation.
- SALARY_MASTER: A comprehensive competency-based salary table sourced from
  DataMasterSalaryRate2026.xlsx, providing 50 roles × 24 levels with full cost
  breakdown (gaji pokok, man-month, man-day, external cost with 30% margin).
  Each level maps to required years of experience per education tier (SMK/D3/S1/S2/S3).

Key Improvements in v6.0:
- Added SALARY_MASTER: Flexible competency-based rate table (50 roles × 24 levels).
- Replaced fixed-cost government personnel budgeting (Rp 20M/person) with
  dynamic lookup based on role, education, and experience.
- Added EDUCATION_TIERS and EDUCATION_EXP_KEY constants.
- Added get_salary_rate() and find_level_by_experience() helper functions.
- Added comprehensive docstrings and comments for clarity.
- Incorporated a robust validation function (validate_data_integrity) to ensure
  consistency between RATE_CARD, TYPICAL_TEAMS, and SALARY_MASTER.
- Implemented standard logging for debugging.
- Added type hinting for better code quality.
"""

